      "postID": "5a005e666ec6491f413480c0",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "Unfortunately \"ghost\" avatars would not increase framerate. Your lag is (once again!) not related to polycount-- most of your framerate loss comes from CPU capping. The CPU is typically capped due to the IK calculations (expensive!), networking overhead (not that expensive), draw calls (somewhat expensive, per-user), and DynamicBones (EXTREMELY expensive, per-user). Unless this \"ghost\" avatar had zero IK calculations, I doubt it would help performance much.\n\nAdditionally, unless this culling would also cull IK/dynamic bones completely (as in, disabled their calculations completely), it would have basically no effect.\n\nAnd, just to reiterate-- \"low poly\" versions of avatars or \"low poly\" ghosts would not affect performance, because polycount does not affect performance. :)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
